       "reason": {
        "description": "Machine-readable failure mode. Declared by this tool: `invalid_query`: query leaves a parenthesis, range bracket or double quote unbalanced, or ends in an escaping backslash (refused before any request); or the portal rejected the query string (invalid query syntax), or answered another 400 the server did not anticipate, whose upstream message is carried. `query_server_error`: Every attempt of a search with query set answered HTTP 500, as the portal does for some malformed queries in place of its 400 syntax rejection. `page_window_exceeded`: page \u00d7 limit exceeds 10,000, the deepest match the portal pages to. `invalid_range`: year_from is after year_to, or min_events is above max_events. `rate_limited`: The portal's 60-a-minute budget is spent: it answered 429, or the request could not start within the call's deadline. data.retryAfter is set. `upstream_unreadable`: The portal answered with a body the server could not read: not JSON, missing the expected envelope, or over the byte ceiling (then data.retryable is false). Also raised when a search answers 404. Other values are possible when a failure originates below the handler.",
        "examples": [
         "invalid_query",
         "query_server_error",
         "page_window_exceeded",
         "invalid_range",
         "rate_limited",
         "upstream_unreadable"
        ],
        "type": "string"
       },
